{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/309334-wtf-pc-game","id":309334,"title":"WtF PC game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-11T11:24:28-08:00","id":309334,"title":"WtF PC game","content":"I'm waiting for second edition and looking for fun and inspiration for it. So I thought that some video gaming in mood would be valid. I know that previous <b>Werewolf</b> game did never really come out - poor <a href=\"http://youtu.be/bYmiwbO5icc\" target=\"_blank\">Heart of Gaia</a> - but maybe you know games at least in part of mood for <b>Forsaken</b>?<br /> <br /> To this day I must say that <i>Wolf Among Us</i>, even if mainly <b>Changeling: the Lost</b> in tone and feel, has protagonists that is having very typical Forsaken problems - he is werewolf with five forms that must guard secret society of beings not known to humans, concerned with anger in him. Just see below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/cXOuqFEbTDw?t=3m\" data-code=\"cXOuqFEbTDw\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/cXOuqFEbTDw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I'm also think that good inspiration could be <i>Legend of Zelda: Twilight Princess </i>- in which Link is kidnaped by some ephemeral weird forces to parallel dimension of spirit and transformed in to wolf form in this realm, where he fight the invasion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/wXNfxBRx1Gk?t=2m18s\" data-code=\"wXNfxBRx1Gk\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wXNfxBRx1Gk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> But the best Shadow Realm was shown in <i>Silent Hill</i> series, especially in <i>SH2</i>. Emotions of residents, literally, makes a Wound in the town's Shadow. Main antagonists are spirit-monster based on characters flaws and vices, represented in very unsettling spiritual beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/XGD88ud5VPk\" data-code=\"XGD88ud5VPk\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XGD88ud5VPk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Still, it's not good enough as <b>THE Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> video game - we have games that are good for being werewolves, or about guarding spirit - but not both. Have any better propositions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-12-2014, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T01:53:50-08:00","id":309988,"title":"","content":"Even the mmorpg about masquerade was cancelled, so, I think a Forsaken videogame will be just a dream BUT.<br /> I freaking love this idea, because WtF is my favourite game here.<br /> Actually I see an option based on videogames and movies :<br /> a typical single player horror chronicle divided in more chapters ( like a pen&amp;paper chronicle) with a lot of animistic horror and urban/sub urban thriller atmosphere.<br /> A mix of Silent Hill, Legacy fo Kain ( yea you know, raziel and the two worlds) and movies like Constantine , but wiht also an atmosphere and a plot like Sons of Anarchy, perfect for matters of territory, retaliation ecc.<br /> The game can focused on a pack maybe of 5 members ( maybe the pack of Elias Winterborn or maybe a pack of Denver, and you can choose and personalize the character you want to play) fighting against a lot of things related to a great enemy (return of an Idigam or something else like the pure tribes).<br /> But the first game I would use for ispiration is, of course, Red Dead Redemption.<br /> And now, why? Red Dead Redemption is wild, is action, is tragedy, is about gangs, about revenge, about.. redemption. And is VERY creepy somethimes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T03:23:09-08:00","id":310024,"title":"","content":"My dream is...<br /> 1) Very complex game (not complicated, but exactly complex) which will completly reflex WoD system (characters need to eat, drink, sleep; day or night, weather, season, clothes and other stuff will have influence on the gameplay).<br /> 2) Influence of the skills, when every new skill is not just dot in charlist but really is new opportunety for character. Something like Fallout<br /> 3) Dynamic combat-system which will culculated the stats of chacarters and NPCs including Initiative. May be something &quot;automatic&quot; like The Witcher.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T03:29:49-08:00","id":310025,"title":"","content":"As to proper &quot;<b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> video game&quot; I'm all in favour. But we probably won't see this in years, if ever... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/309334-wtf-pc-game?p=309988#post309988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the first game I would use for ispiration is, of course, Red Dead Redemption.<br /> And now, why? Red Dead Redemption is wild, is action, is tragedy, is about gangs, about revenge, about.. redemption. And is VERY creepy somethimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't play the game, per se, ( I don't have XBox ) but I watched enought Youtube clips about it so I could probably as I played. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>Red Dead Redeption</i>, for me, is great for <b>Deadlands</b> ( great western, with <i><b>ZOMBIES!</b></i> in DLC <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) but I doubt it's good for <b>Forsaken</b> themes. Uratha don't do revange, they have <i>duty </i>from Wolf and Moon. They don't need redemption, becuase it's not theier sins need to be fixed - rather they forfathers. It's more about legacy. And John Marston isn't part of the pack, really. He fights gangs, sure, but by himself. Not to mention there aren't any animistic undertones in the game. And no werewolves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-12-2014, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T03:35:16-08:00","id":310027,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, OP does not hold the rights to the WoD IP. Otherwise, I would suggest allowing small-ish, indy studios to use the IP to create games based in the World of Darkness. Heck, I bet Obsidian would love to do a Vampire game if they could get CCP on board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T06:23:12-08:00","id":311150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/309334-wtf-pc-game?p=310025#post310025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Red Dead Redeption</i>, for me, is great for <b>Deadlands</b> ( great western, with <i><b>ZOMBIES!</b></i> in DLC <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) but I doubt it's good for <b>Forsaken</b> themes. Uratha don't do revange, they have <i>duty </i>from Wolf and Moon. They don't need redemption, becuase it's not theier sins need to be fixed - rather they forfathers. It's more about legacy. And John Marston isn't part of the pack, really. He fights gangs, sure, but by himself. Not to mention there aren't any animistic undertones in the game. And no werewolves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that Werewolf the Forsaken (videogame) MUST be LIKE RDR, I'm just saying that I saw a lot of cool components in RDR <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Like for example:<br /> - Of course, gangs fight. In a possible WtF game you are not alone. You have a pack. You are a gang, actually .<br /> - Redemption: yes, their redemption actually <i>is </i>their <i>duty.</i><br /> - Wild zones: RDR have a lot of cool places like Tall Trees or Cholla Springs (very creepy during night)<br /> - Revenge: the hate-cult of the pure tribes is actually based on hate <i>and</i> revenge.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that it must be like RDR <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But it could be a good game to find some inspirations in matter of locations and social relationships (Pure tribes, small villages in the woods ecc..).<br /> The ''mood'' is pretty wild and harsh.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}